      "id": "B02",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "reason": "Read invalidates lastRead before copying zero bytes and returns (0, nil). UnreadByte rejects that state. A subsequent successful ReadByte sets lastRead to opRead and advances the offset, so UnreadByte succeeds and decrements the offset, allowing the same byte to be read again. TestBufferZeroReadInvalidatesUnread asserts the entire sequence, including both reads of 'b'.",
      "line": 431,
      "fragment": "func (b *Buffer) UnreadByte() error {\n\tif b.lastRead == opInvalid {\n\t\treturn errUnreadByte\n\t}\n\tb.lastRead = opInvalid\n\tif b.off > 0 {\n\t\tb.off--\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}"
    }
  ]
